MAJOR_VERSION=4
STANDARD_VERSION=2
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=14
DESCRIPTION<<VER_END
PRE 4.2.0: Wi-Fi scan home SSID + SSID-based join; Codex security fixes

- wifi scan (lab backend): reads FL_NET_WIFI_HOME_SSID env var and includes the
  user's home network in scan results; FL_NET_WIFI_HOME_AUTH (open/wpa2/wpa3)
  and FL_NET_WIFI_HOME_BAND (2/5/6) are optional — defaults are wpa2 and 2.4 GHz
- wifi join: lab backend no longer requires the target SSID to appear in the last
  scan; if the network is absent a synthetic scan entry is built from the supplied
  SSID + password so home and hidden networks can be joined directly by name
- wifi join usage: clarified as `wifi join <ssid> [password]`; BSSID option
  shown on its own line as an advanced pin-to-AP flag, no longer top-billed
- security: shell-escape SSID and passphrase before popen nmcli/wpa_cli calls
  (shell injection via crafted SSID or passphrase — net_wifi_host_linux.c)
- security: reject sparse file-transfer chunks whose file_offset != bytes already
  received; also reject chunks that exceed the advertised file size
  (uninitialized-memory write to disk via out-of-order chunks — net_file_delivery.c)
- fix: preserve statted file_size across fl_server_file_offer_create memset so
  total_chunks is not always zero (cmd_server_file.c)
- fix: add missing braces in fl_net_sock_native_close so listener sockets do not
  close tcp_conn_id 0 or call stack_unlock without a matching lock (net_sock_native.c)
VER_END

RELEASE_DATE=2026-06-14
